<title>UK: National Power ups stake in Pakistan plant.</title>
<headline>National Power ups stake in Pakistan plant.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>British electricity generator National Power Plc said it had signed a share purchase agreement to take an extra 10 percent stake in the Kot Addu Power Company (KAPCO) for $76 million.</p>
<p>In a statement, the company said KAPCO owns a 1,600 MegaWatt oil and gas-fired combined cycle plant in Pakistan.</p>
</text>
